  "rules": [
    "Only buy while the hourly close is above the 200-hour EMA.",
    "Buy when the MACD line (12, 26) crosses above its 9-period signal line while both are below zero.",
    "Put the stop at the 200-hour EMA and the target at 1.5 times the risk.",
    "Risking the same 20 USDT per trade: a stop closer than 1% is widened to 1% and one wider than 15% is cut to 15%, so a position never passes 2,000 USDT.",
    "Hold one position per coin at a time."
  ],
  "notExpressed": [
    "TradingLab calls it the 200-day moving average without a type; the test uses the 200 EMA on the trading chart, as Trading Rush does",
    "Trading Rush's own trades take a quarter off at 1R, move the stop to breakeven and aim for 2R; its 100-trade test used the flat 1.5R kept here",
    "Waiting for price to come back to a support level first (TradingLab's optional filter)",
    "The source trades its own chart timeframe on forex or stocks; the test runs it on hourly crypto candles",
    "Short trades below the 200 EMA (the test is spot, long only)"
